  "description": "EQIFAO crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H116 Mn1 O38 Y6 1+,6(C1 H4 O1),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y5 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y6 (Y) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.483-3.759 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.18-106.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [MnY6(OH)8(o-tol)12(MeOH)6]Cl·6MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
